  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This medium-sized tree has unusual foliage. The leaves emerge as a pale yellowish green, turning to a light, bright green as they mature. They do not form a flat plane as most forms do, but the lobes bend up or down slightly, or some lobes twist slightly. Some leaves hang down, some flat, some on edge, creating a foliage cover toothing between the notches. This shorter type of tree tends to grow rather broad and not strongly upright, reaching 3-4 m high. The total foliage appearance is rather feathery. Another name by which this cultivar has been known is"
  },
